EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key

# --- Phase 3A-3D: Solana/USDC payment infrastructure ---
# All optional, all safe as EXPO_PUBLIC_* (client-exposed): reading public
# blockchain data and knowing which network to target require no secret.
# Never add a privileged RPC provider API key here -- see the Phase 3A
# design doc's Decision 4/Decision 1 for why that must stay server-side
# (the verify-payment Edge Function has its own separate, non-public
# SOLANA_NETWORK/SOLANA_RPC_URL secrets -- see below).
#
# As of Phase 3D, real payments ARE wired in end to end (public checkout ->
# Pay with Wallet -> verify-payment Edge Function -> Postgres). These
# variables control the CLIENT half of that: which network the "Pay with
# Wallet" Solana Pay link targets. They must be kept in sync with the
# server's own SOLANA_NETWORK secret (see docs/superpowers/
# phase-3e-production-readiness.md) -- a mismatch fails safe (verification
# simply never matches) but silently, not with a clear error.

# 'devnet' (default if unset) or 'mainnet-beta'. A production build must
# explicitly opt into mainnet-beta -- never make this default to mainnet.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SOLANA_NETWORK=devnet

# Overrides the default public Solana cluster endpoint (e.g. to point at a
# paid RPC provider's URL). Leave unset to use Solana's free public RPC.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL=

# 'mock' (default if unset) or 'real'. See src/services/blockchain/solana/paymentMode.ts.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_PAYMENT_MODE=mock

# --- Phase 3B: public checkout link base URL ---
# The domain used to build shareable /p/<token> checkout links (see
# src/utils/publicPaymentLink.ts). Defaults to https://pay.speropay.app,
# which is aspirational -- this project has not been deployed anywhere yet.
# Set this once a real HTTPS deployment exists.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CHECKOUT_BASE_URL=https://pay.speropay.app

# --- Phase 5B: Google Play listing, for the web-only landing screen ---
# Spero's real product is the native Android app; the web deployment at
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CHECKOUT_BASE_URL only serves /p, /c, and a lightweight
# landing page for every other route (see src/utils/webRouteGuard.ts). This
# is unset until a real Play Store listing exists -- see
# src/utils/googlePlayUrl.ts. Leaving it unset shows "Coming soon to Google
# Play" instead of a link; never set this to a placeholder/fake URL.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PLAY_URL=https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.speropay.app
